1
00:00:05,842 --> 00:00:07,552
(Leonard:)I don't get how she can just announce...

2
00:00:07,719 --> 00:00:10,009
...that an old boyfriend is gonna sleep
on her couch.

3
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:12,600
(Sheldon:)Hey, I thought of a game
we can play in the car.

4
00:00:12,766 --> 00:00:14,146
I don't wanna play a game, Sheldon.

5
00:00:14,309 --> 00:00:17,439
(Sheldon:)It's called Scientists.
Now, I will name three scientists...

6
00:00:17,604 --> 00:00:21,484
...you'll put them in order of the size
of their contribution to their fields.

7
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:23,400
(Sheldon:)To make this game
even more compelling...

8
00:00:23,568 --> 00:00:26,908
(Sheldon:)...you must consider only the
contribution of the man to the field...

9
00:00:27,072 --> 00:00:29,032
(Sheldon:)...not the validity of the field itself.

10
00:00:29,199 --> 00:00:31,409
(Sheldon:)For example,
Abu Musa Jabir ibn Hayyan...

11
00:00:31,576 --> 00:00:34,916
(Sheldon:)...made a greater contribution
to the discredited field of alchemy...

12
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,460
(Sheldon:)...than Halbert Vanderplatt
made to neurobiology.

13
00:00:37,624 --> 00:00:39,544
(Sheldon:)Okay. Ready to have some fun?

14
00:00:40,794 --> 00:00:42,874
(Leonard:)An old boyfriend
who's "definitely not gay."

15
00:00:43,046 --> 00:00:45,886
You know, that's what a guy
likes to hear. "Definitely."

16
00:00:46,049 --> 00:00:47,629
(Sheldon:)All right, I'll start with an easy one.

17
00:00:47,801 --> 00:00:51,591
(Sheldon:)Um, Isaac Newton, Madame Curie
and Niels Bohr.

18
00:00:51,763 --> 00:00:55,103
(Leonard:)And then I say one little thing
and I end up being the bad guy.

19
00:00:55,267 --> 00:00:58,437
(Sheldon:)Hint. Madame Curie had her husband
to help her.

20
00:00:58,603 --> 00:00:59,893
(Leonard:)What am I supposed to say?

21
00:01:00,063 --> 00:01:03,273
"Sure, Penny. I'm cool with your old
boyfriend sleeping in your apartment."

